  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Senegal: Enhancing Judicial Capacity for Alternatives to Incarceration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: National School of Penitentiary Administration (&#xc9;cole nationale d&apos;administration p&#xe9;nitentiaire &#x2013; ENAP).Indirect beneficiaries: Justice seekers in Senegal, particularly women and young adults, and the broader Senegalese prison population.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to enable criminal justice actors to use alternatives to incarceration and social reintegration mechanisms to reduce overcrowding and poor conditions in Senegalese prisons.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To ensure that the Senegalese Judiciary, and particularly the sentence enforcement judges, have the necessary knowledge and resources to promote alternatives to incarceration solutions in their beneficiaries&#x2019; cases.</narrative>
  </description>
